From: mscharged-port
Subject: Rollback: a step's deterministic data goes out once, from whichever run queues it
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Tweak patch 0029 dropped every deterministic data packet a replayed step
queued, as having gone out when the step first ran. With predicted inputs
the first run may not have queued it: the host's camera ends a slow motion
(GameplayCameraEffects::Reset, cGame::SendSlowDownEnd) at a step whose
first run, on inputs predicted wrong, had not reached that end yet, and
reaches it in the replay. The replay dropped the end and the camera, which
no longer owned the time scale, never sent it again: every machine stayed
in the slow motion, together and without a desync, for the rest of the
match.

InputRouter::QueueDetermData now asks the rollback whether the step sent
those bytes already (mscharged_rollback_determ_data_new): the rollback
keeps, outside the memory it restores, what each step it tracks sent in
any of its runs, and a later run, a replay or the step run again after it
was undone, sends only what is not there. A packet a replay queues again
stays out as before; one only the replay queues goes out, a step later
than the original would have. The packets the host sends from predicted
steps are state the game takes as the latest (the players' visibility,
every ten steps) or ignores when it changes nothing (a slow motion's end
with the time scale at 1), so one sent from a replay as well as from the
first run is harmless. Outside tracked steps everything goes out.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_rollback.h b/include/mscharged_rollback.h
index b3488c3c..93d0c1c6 100644
--- a/include/mscharged_rollback.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_rollback.h
@@ -38,6 +38,14 @@ bool mscharged_rollback_active(void);
 // Whether the steps running now replay earlier ones: deterministic data they
 // queue was sent when they first ran.
 bool mscharged_rollback_resimulating(void);
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// Whether deterministic data a step queues goes out: once for each step, by
+// its bytes. A replay sends what the step's earlier runs did not (with
+// predicted inputs, its first run may not have queued it: the host's end of
+// a slow motion), and drops what went out already; so does a step run again
+// after it was undone. Outside tracked steps, everything goes out.
+bool mscharged_rollback_determ_data_new(int frame, const void* data, unsigned size);
+#endif
 // The inputs applied for the step about to run.
 void mscharged_rollback_inputs_applied(const struct MschargedRollbackInputs* inputs);
 // Between two fixed steps of a match, where the rollback saves the match and
diff --git a/src/Game/InputRouter.cpp b/src/Game/InputRouter.cpp
index 761603a0..1ecb100b 100644
--- a/src/Game/InputRouter.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/InputRouter.cpp
@@ -333,20 +333,20 @@ void InputRouter::QueueDetermData(const void* data, u32 size)
 {
 #if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
     if (mscharged_rollback_active())
     {
         // RECHARGED_NET_DEBUG: what the steps queue, sent or not, by type
         // (its first byte) and step.
         const unsigned type = size > 0 ? *static_cast<const u8*>(data) : 0;
         const int frame = gInputManager != 0 ? gInputManager->mFrameProvider->GetFrame() : -1;
-        // A replayed step: its data went out when the step first ran.
-        if (mscharged_rollback_resimulating())
+        // Once for each step: what a run of it sent before stays out.
+        if (!mscharged_rollback_determ_data_new(frame, data, size))
         {
-            tDebugPrintManager::Print(DC_NETWORK, "Determ data %u of step %d not sent: a replay\n", type, frame);
+            tDebugPrintManager::Print(DC_NETWORK, "Determ data %u of step %d not sent: sent before\n", type, frame);
             return;
         }
         DetermDataEvent* outgoing = ::new (malloc(sizeof(DetermDataEvent))) DetermDataEvent(data, size);
         if (!m_OutgoingCustomDetermDataQ.IsFull())
         {
             m_OutgoingCustomDetermDataQ.Push(outgoing);
             tDebugPrintManager::Print(DC_NETWORK, "Determ data %u of step %d queued\n", type, frame);
         }
